return {
  summary = "Log in, get a Trainer ID, add friends in-game, and see their last-known positions - async, plain-HTTP presence, no server process required (Android-friendly).",
  author = "Ash",
  tags = { "multiplayer", "online", "overworld", "presence" },
  differences = {
    added = {
      "Pokemon Crystal support: the launcher added Crystal as a new Beta-status Gen 2 game (confirmed directly against the engine's own src/core/GameVersion.lua - Gold and Silver have since had their own \"(Beta)\" launcher label dropped entirely, no longer Beta). game.save.version now also recognizes \"crystal\" alongside red/blue/yellow/gold/silver (resolveGameVersion), and isGen2() treats CRYSTAL exactly like GOLD/SILVER - confirmed by reading the engine's actual src/core/gen2/Save.lua that Crystal shares that exact same module and save-field layout (money, badges, pokedex, hallOfFame all read identically); Crystal's own extras (save.crystal, save.battleTower) are separate fields this mod has no reason to touch. Server-side, ping.php/stats.php/schema.sql/online_by_version.php and every public_*.php leaderboard/stats endpoint now all track CRYSTAL alongside RED/BLUE/YELLOW/GOLD/SILVER; the website gained a Crystal swatch colour and label. No database schema/migration needed - game_version is a plain VARCHAR(16), not an enum.",
      "Gym signs: every gym across all three supported runs (Gen1 Kanto, Gen2 Johto, Gen2 Kanto) now gets its own sign - not a Victory Road badge gate, a separate friendly NPC - listing which of your ACCEPTED friends already hold that specific gym's badge (\"NO FRIENDS HAVE THIS BADGE YET\" if none do). Placement is discovered at runtime via mod.world:mapOverview()'s live collision snapshot, searching a small plus/3x3 neighbourhood around wherever YOU yourself just walked in (mod.world:current()) for the first walkable, non-warp, unoccupied tile - never a hardcoded coordinate, since this project ships no ROM data. Backed by a new per-account badges_mask (one bit per specific badge, uploaded alongside the existing stats snapshot) so this can answer \"does this friend have THIS badge\" rather than just a plain count.",
      "League leaderboard sign: a second new sign near the Elite Four entrance (INDIGO_PLATEAU_LOBBY) ranks total league clears - SUM(league_wins) across every game_version an account has played, one combined number per person. Two pages (ALL PLAYERS top 50 / FRIENDS-only), toggled LEFT/RIGHT, each sorted by SELECT between descending (top scorer first) and ascending. Server-computed names/Trainer IDs/numbers only - no free text of any kind, same no-chat/no-DM policy this project has always followed. Registered unconditionally (works the same in Gen1); on Gen2, where this exact map id isn't yet confirmed to exist, the whole spawn attempt is wrapped in pcall and silently no-ops instead of guessing a map id.",
      "Gen 2 (Gold/Silver, currently Beta in the launcher) support: SilphNet now declares \"games\": [\"gen1\", \"gen2\"] and sends a real GOLD/SILVER game_version instead of collapsing it to UNKNOWN. Friend markers, presence, the friends list, add/remove/accept-friend, and party all work unchanged - those are already generation-agnostic parts of the mod API. Stats reading was updated for three genuine save-shape differences confirmed directly against the engine's own src/core/gen2/Save.lua: money lives at save.player.money on Gen 2 (not top-level save.money), badges come from save.player.badges + save.player.kantoBadges (16 total, no badge items in the inventory at all on Gen 2), and league wins read save.hallOfFame.count (a table, not save.hallOfFame's Gen 1 plain array). Pokedex-caught reads save.pokedex.caught on Gen 2 instead of .owned (.seen is unchanged on both). Server-side, ping.php/stats.php/schema.sql/online_by_version.php now all track SILVER alongside GOLD, RED, BLUE and YELLOW.",
      "HTTP requests are async again. A newer Gen1Recomp engine build shipped mod.fetch - a real, documented replacement for the love.thread capability an earlier update permanently blocked (see v1.9.0's fix below): mod.fetch:get() returns a handle immediately and mod.fetch:poll() never blocks, with the engine's own worker threads doing the actual network I/O rather than the mod's code, so this restores asynchrony without reopening the hole love.thread would have. Presence pings, the friends/pending/online-count/nearby/online-by-version fetches, add/remove/accept-friend, friend detail, and stats/activity uploads all now go through this path - the game no longer visibly pauses for these while mod.fetch is available. Automatically falls back to the exact v1.9.0 synchronous behaviour (same visible pause, same 2.5s cap) on any build or permission set where mod.fetch isn't available, so nothing breaks on an older engine. Login, registration, and cached-token reconnect stay fully synchronous unconditionally either way - mod.fetch is GET-only, and a password (or a bare session token with nothing else attached) must never be sent as part of a URL.",
      "mod.fetch's real 4-requests-in-flight-per-mod ceiling is now handled gracefully: the ~30s presence cycle alone fires 5 requests at once (ping, friends, pending, online count, nearby), so the 5th now waits its turn in a small queue and is submitted the moment any of the other four completes, rather than being dropped or erroring out.",
      "Trainer ID: a unique 5-digit id (00000-65535, same range as the mainline games) assigned once at registration and shown on the status screen - the key used to add friends in-game.",
      "In-game Add Friend screen: a D-pad digit spinner (UP/DOWN changes a digit, LEFT/RIGHT moves the cursor, A sends the request) - no typing, no web page, just enter a friend's Trainer ID.",
      "Incoming friend requests: polled on the same ~30s cycle as presence, shown as a REQUESTS count on the status screen, paged through and accepted on their own screen (LEFT from the status screen).",
      "GitHub auto-update: manifest.json now sets \"github\" so the launcher's Update / Other Versions can pull new releases directly - see .github/workflows/release-silphnet.yml (packages only mod/silphnet/, never the server source or docs, as a GitHub Release .zip on every push to main that touches the mod).",
      "Friend markers show their name: press A on a friend's map marker to see who it is, in a small text box that closes on A or B - a live lookup done at the moment you press A, not baked in when the marker appeared.",
      "Friends list now shows each friend's Trainer ID, and a LEFT/RIGHT:PAGE hint when you have more than one friend.",
      "Global online count: shown on the status screen's FRIENDS line (\"FRIENDSn ONn\") - everyone currently online, not just friends.",
      "NEARBY: a second Start Menu row (\"SN NEARBY\") opens its own screen showing everyone else currently on your own map, by name and Trainer ID, titled with how many people are there and the map name - Pokemon-Go-style. Shows ALREADY A FRIEND for someone you've added, or NOT YET A FRIEND with a reminder to add them the normal way (RIGHT from the SilphNet status screen) using the Trainer ID shown.",
      "Friend detail screen: press A on a friend in the friends list to see their self-reported stats (badges, Pokedex seen/caught, League wins, money) and latest activity - a real, event-driven catch message on two lines (\"CAUGHT LVL 25\" / \"BLASTOISE\") with its own time-ago, plus last-seen repeated from the main friends list. Stats upload on a slower ~3 min cycle than presence; activity uploads immediately on the real pokemon.caught event, not a poll. Badge count is derived from save.inventory checked against the constants.badges registry (Badges.count() itself isn't mod-accessible) - a faithful reimplementation of the engine's own internal logic, confirmed against its real source rather than guessed.",
      "Real game version detection: game.save.version (\"red\"/\"blue\"/\"yellow\"/\"gold\", confirmed directly from SaveData.lua's own save-table construction, guaranteed non-nil by an engine migration) now populates gameVersion, replacing the permanent \"UNKNOWN\" placeholder that had sat unverified since early in the project. The friends list shows an online friend's current version on the page-counter line (\"1/3 (BLUE)\", hidden while offline); the friend detail screen shows every version with real data as its own set of pages in one flat A-press cycle (see below).",
      "Time Played on the friend detail STATS page (\"TIME 34H 12M\") - reads game.save.playTime, which has two possible shapes engine-side (a plain seconds count, or an {hours,minutes,seconds,frames} table), normalized client-side into one total-seconds value before upload.",
      "Party page on the friend detail screen: cycle to PARTY (via A, alongside STATS/ACTIVITY) to see a friend's party, one mon per screen (species, level, current/max HP, up to 4 moves), paged with LEFT/RIGHT. No sprite - the mod API has no documented way to draw a species sprite outside the overworld NPC marker system, only text, so this stays text-only like every other screen. Encoded client-side as one compact delimited string (not JSON) and stored in a new friend_stats.party column, following this project's existing \"no JSON library available\" convention.",
      "SN ONLINE: a new Start Menu row/screen showing who's online across the WHOLE service, grouped by game version - a summary page (\"RED n ON\" / \"BLUE n ON\" / \"YELLOW n ON\", LEFT/RIGHT to open one), then each version's own page listing exactly who's online in it, one person per screen (UP/DOWN pages between them) - same ALREADY A FRIEND / NOT YET A FRIEND + add-by-Trainer-ID flow SN NEARBY already uses, just scoped to a game version instead of a map. Built on a new online_by_version.php endpoint (excludes the caller, excludes UNKNOWN-version rows entirely - see that file's own comments for why).",
    },
    changed = {
      "Server-side: ping.php, nearby.php, stats.php, friend_detail.php, add_friend.php, remove_friend.php, and accept_friend.php now accept their fields via GET querystring as well as POST (matching the pattern friends.php/pending_requests.php/online_count.php already used) - required so mod.fetch, which is GET-only, can reach them. Self-hosters upgrading server/web/api/ need these updated files; login.php/register.php/login_token.php are unchanged and still POST-only.",
      "Status screen controls swapped once logged in: A now opens the friends list (was START), START is now re-auth (was A's secondary job). Pre-login, A still retries login / confirms account creation exactly as before - only the post-login bindings changed.",
      "Start Menu labels shortened from \"SILPHNET\" to \"SN\" (e.g. \"SN ASHJAM\", \"SN NEARBY\", \"SN SET NAME/PASS\") - some third-party UI mods truncate long Start Menu rows by chopping off anything past a length limit rather than adding an ellipsis, so a longer label could disappear entirely depending on name length. The full-screen status title (\"- SILPHNET -\") is unchanged since that's a roomier context.",
      "Friends list: A now opens the new friend detail screen instead of paging to the next friend - paging moved to DPAD LEFT/RIGHT only (SELECT:REMOVE is unchanged), same convention the Nearby screen already used.",
      "Friend detail screen redesigned: A is now the ONLY navigation button, cycling in one flat loop through every version's STATS page, then that version's ACTIVITY page, then the next version's STATS/ACTIVITY, wrapping back to the start - replacing an interim two-axis LEFT/RIGHT-for-page-type plus SELECT-for-version scheme this same version briefly shipped with internally before this correction. A version only gets pages in the cycle if it has real stats or activity data - presence-only versions (pinged but never reported stats) don't appear. The game version is now shown on its own line under the page title (\"ARCHADA STATS\" / \"BLUE\") for every friend, not just multi-version ones.",
    },
    fixed = {
      "A friend's ACTIVITY message could show only a mangled first line and nothing on the second - reported directly (\"CAUGHT LVL 56\" then what looked like garbage where the species name should be). Root cause: this file's hand-rolled JSON field extraction (objectsFromArrayBody, nestedObj, jsonField) never decoded JSON string escapes at all - a genuine newline in the activity message (see queueCatchActivity) survives the server round-trip correctly (confirmed directly via a real SQL check against friend_activity.message - the database always had it right), but PHP's json_encode() represents that newline in the JSON text as the two literal characters \\ and n, and this file's plain gmatch captures were reading that AS TEXT instead of decoding it back into a real line break. Same root cause would also have broken a Gen 2 gendered species name's own gender glyph the first time a friend's activity or party page tried to show one (silphnet_json() calls json_encode() with no JSON_UNESCAPED_UNICODE, so any non-ASCII byte - including \\xE2\\x99\\x82/\\x80 - comes across as a \\uXXXX escape too), just not reported yet. Added a real jsonUnescapeString() decoder (handles \\n/\\t/\\r/\\b/\\f/\\\"/\\\\/\\/ and \\uXXXX, the exact set PHP's json_encode can produce) and wired it into every place this file pulls a string value out of JSON.",
      "SN ONLINE's summary page no longer overlaps its own footer hints. It used to list every tracked version's count on one page, one row per version (16px apart) - fine for 3-5 versions, but Crystal made a 6th row that landed exactly on top of the \"LR:VERSION\" hint text, reported directly as \"Crystal has now been pushed down and is overlapping the mappings at the bottom.\" Split into two summary pages by generation instead of shrinking rows to fit: a Gen 1 page (RED/BLUE/YELLOW) and a Gen 2 page (GOLD/SILVER/CRYSTAL), each with a \"TOTAL ONLINE\" figure that's the SAME combined count across every game on both pages (not just that half), per direct request. The per-version player-list pages (where the START:ADD FRIEND shortcut lives) are unchanged, just renumbered to come after both summary pages instead of one.",
      "SN LEAGUE CLEARS' per-row rank line no longer shows two numbers that usually say the same thing. It used to read \"#<rank>  <index>/<n>\" - rank and browsing position ARE the same number whenever the list is sorted descending (the default), which is most of the time, so a 2-entry list showed something like \"#1  1/2\" and \"#2  2/2\" - reported directly as \"just looks a bit untidy and repetitive.\" v1.13.1's fix (\"#<rank> OF <n>\") shipped with a real bug of its own, caught on-device after committing rather than before: this engine's font has no real \"#\" glyph at all - confirmed against src/render/Font.lua - it's a deliberate macro that expands \"#\" to the literal 4-character \"POKe\" (accented), mirroring the real cartridge's own charmap quirk where the ROM's font has one character code for the whole \"POKe\" string. It rendered on the real screen as \"POKe1   1/2\" instead of \"#1  1/2\", reported directly as looking wrong (\"That isn't the persons username, that's underneath\"). Final wording, as of this version, is \"RANK <rank> OF <n>\" - no symbol, same information, no macro collision.",
      "league_wins can no longer be dragged back down once an account has genuinely earned a higher number - server-side (stats.php), the column is now updated with GREATEST(new value, stored value) instead of a plain overwrite. This is the answer to \"can we trigger something to increment the number\": rather than trying to catch the exact moment a champion battle is won client-side (the engine has no single clean event for that - world.trainer_engaged knows WHO you're fighting but not the outcome, battle.ended knows the outcome but not who - correctly stitching those together to avoid a double-count risk was judged too fragile to ship without dedicated testing), this makes the EXISTING count a one-way ratchet instead: once the server has ever recorded N clears for an account, no future client report - including a smaller number caused by a later .sav re-import wiping game.save.hallOfFame again - can ever push it back below N. Only league_wins gets this treatment; badges/pokedex/money/play_seconds all remain plain overwrites since the .sav codec does preserve those correctly and a silent floor on a field that's never actually needed one would just hide a real future bug instead of a real limitation. Server-only change - no client/mod update or database schema change required, just re-upload stats.php.",
      "Found and fixed the real root cause of \"YOUR CLEARS shows 0 despite genuinely beating the league\" (Gen 1 only): a save that's ever been through the launcher's .sav import/export feature silently loses its Hall of Fame roster entirely - confirmed directly against the engine's own save-conversion codec (src/save_convert/GenSave.lua, 1146 lines) that this format has NO handling of Hall of Fame data at all, in either direction, unlike ordinary continuing play which preserves it fine. leagueWins now also checks save.flags.EVENT_BEAT_CHAMPION_RIVAL - a permanent, never-cleared flag the game's own story scripts set once and which the .sav codec's eventFlags crosswalk DOES preserve - and floors the count at 1 if the roster reads empty but this flag says the champion has genuinely been beaten. This can only ever recover \"at least 1\", never a true original count lost before an import (a boolean flag can't carry a count) - but every real clear from here on, with no further imports, still increments normally on top of that floor. Gen 2 is unaffected (no .sav import path exists for Gold/Silver in this engine).",
      "Stats upload now logs the exact snapshot it sends (version, league wins, badges) every time one goes out - added while tracking down the bug above, kept as a standing diagnostic.",
      "Gym sign / league leaderboard sign no longer spawns right in the doorway. It used to search only the 8 tiles immediately touching the player's own entry tile - which IS the doorway - so the sign landed exactly where a real player needs to walk through a second later. It now uses the player's own entry facing to project a few tiles deeper into the room first, then searches beside that line (not directly on it), before ever falling back to the old right-beside-you search - still zero hardcoded coordinates, every candidate tile is still verified walkable live via mod.world:mapOverview().",
      "League leaderboard sign screen's bottom button hints (\"LR:LIST SEL:SORT\" / \"B:BACK\") were sitting right on top of the screen's own bottom border instead of below it, making them look chopped off - the box was sized to its own content (20x11 tiles) instead of the full 20x18 every other screen in this mod uses, and drawBox's border occupies its very last row. Both the gym sign and league sign screens now use the same full-height box every other screen already does, with real clearance before the footer.",
      "League leaderboard sign screen now also shows your own total league clears (\"YOUR CLEARS n\"), and a persistent \"SN LEAGUE CLEARS\" title line so it's clear at a glance what the screen is even about - previously only said \"ALL PLAYERS\"/\"FRIENDS\" with no indication these were clear counts.",
      "\"YOUR CLEARS\" now shows the SAME combined-across-all-your-saves total the leaderboard itself ranks by, not just the one save you're currently standing in. It briefly showed only the current save's own count, which could read as \"0\" (or a smaller number) right next to a leaderboard that already credited the account with a bigger combined total from a different save - reported as \"it says 0, but I have beaten the league\" (true for that one cartridge, not for the account overall). This also means an account with any real combined clears now reliably appears in the ALL PLAYERS list itself, not just in its own \"YOUR CLEARS\" line - it was never deliberately excluded, it just wasn't visible as a person's own number before.",
      "Gym/league sign placement search widened (side range 1-3, was 1-2; search depth 2-8, was 2-6) after a real report of a gym sign landing on top of a statue. This is a mitigation, not a guarantee - see the \"known\" section below for why this project has no way to detect a statue's exact position at all, and how a specific reported overlap can be permanently excluded going forward.",
      "Standing still no longer eventually shows you as OFFLINE to friends. The 30s presence-ping timer was only ever ticked from the real world.stepped event, which the engine only fires on an actual step - so simply stopping walking silently stopped the ping cycle too, and last_seen would eventually fall outside the server's 300s online window even with the game genuinely still open. Now also ticked from the core.update hook, confirmed directly against the engine's own src/core/PlatformHooks.lua to wrap the game's per-frame update regardless of movement - the ping still only actually fires once a real 30 seconds have passed, standing still or not. The server-side \"offline after ~5 minutes of no ping\" rule itself is unchanged.",
      "A Gen 2 species with a spelled-out gender suffix (e.g. OINKOLOGNE_FEMALE, 17 chars) could overflow the 16-char/line budget on its own and get silently truncated mid-word - confirmed by a real friend_activity row reading \"OINKOLOGNE_FEMAL\". Now shown as the real \xE2\x99\x82/\xE2\x99\x80 gender glyph instead (\"OINKOLOGNE\xE2\x99\x80\", 12 chars) everywhere a species name is drawn - the same symbol the real cartridges use for NIDORAN's two forms, confirmed drawable via the engine's own Font.lua. Gen 1's existing short _M/_F convention (NIDORAN_M/NIDORAN_F) is untouched - only a full _MALE/_FEMALE suffix is reformatted.",
      "SN ONLINE's version paging (LEFT/RIGHT between the summary page and each version's own page) had a hardcoded 4-page wrap, silently assuming exactly 3 tracked versions (RED/BLUE/YELLOW) plus the summary page. Found while adding GOLD/SILVER as a 4th and 5th tracked version to online_by_version.php - RIGHT from the last page would have wrapped one page early, making the newest version unreachable. Now computed from however many versions the server actually returns.",
      "About Silphnet no longer closes the Start Menu/options screen entirely when selected. It used to live as an \"ABOUT SILPHNET\" row on the mod manager's own OPTIONS screen, pushing the in-game SilphNetAbout screen from there - that push didn't behave the way the same push does from the Start Menu, and selecting it just closed the menu instead of opening About. Moved to its own \"SN ABOUT\" Start Menu row instead, the same already-working push site SN ASHJAM/SN NEARBY use. The About screen itself now also shows GitHub (ASHJAMB), Instagram (@ASHJAMGRAM), and TikTok (@ASHJAM) alongside the existing name/site/thanks/version - no Discord row yet, added once one exists.",
      "Start Menu label could go stale: if login finished while the player was standing still at boot (before any world.stepped event drained the HTTP result), the \"SN ...\" row wouldn't update to \"SN <name>\" until something else happened to drain the result first - e.g. opening and leaving the status screen. The Start Menu hook now drains pending HTTP results itself before computing the label, so the very first menu open after a completed login already shows the right name.",
      "Old UNKNOWN game_version rows no longer get orphaned once a player updates to this version. game_version is part of the primary key on presence/friend_stats/friend_activity, so a plain upsert keyed on the newly-detected real version couldn't touch the old UNKNOWN row - it would insert a SECOND row instead, leaving the first behind as dead data forever. ping.php now re-keys an account's existing UNKNOWN row onto the real version the moment it's known (once per account, automatically, on that account's next ping after updating) - no manual database cleanup needed. See migrations.sql for the full explanation and how to check progress.",
      "Friends list bottom rows no longer look squashed. Moving the friend N/M counter onto the title line (alongside \"FRIENDS\" - \"FRIENDS 1/3\") freed exactly one 8px row that used to be its own separate line; that row is now used as real clearance between the last data line (\"N HR AGO\") and the hint block below, which is what was actually reported as squashed - not the name/ID/status rows, which keep their original spacing. A:DETAIL and LEFT/RIGHT:PAGE are now combined onto one hint line (\"A:DETAIL LR:PAGE\") since this screen was already at its 144px display limit with 3 separate hint lines and had no other row to spare for the fix. The online version tag (introduced in 1.6.0) moved off the title line onto the ONLINE/OFFLINE line itself (\"ONLINE (BLUE)\") - reads more naturally there, and left enough room on the title line to restore the \"FRIENDS\" text once the version tag no longer needed the space.",
      "Status screen's A:FRIENDS hint no longer shows a placeholder online count. It used to always show something in brackets - \"(- ON)\" before the first online-count fetch landed, or \"(0 ON)\" once it landed with nobody online - which read as a stuck feature rather than a real indicator. The \"(N ON)\" suffix is now dropped entirely whenever there's nobody online, appearing only once there's a genuine positive count to report.",
      "Online counter split in two, fixing a real point of confusion reported directly: with zero friends online but the player themselves within the 5-minute ONLINE window, the status screen showed \"A:FRIENDS(1 ON)\" right next to a friends list where every friend read OFFLINE - correct by that count's original GLOBAL (everyone, self included) definition, but easy to misread as \"one of my friends is online\" sitting where it did. The status screen's A:FRIENDS hint now shows a FRIENDS-ONLY online count instead (computed client-side from the friends list already on-device, no extra network round-trip), so it only ever answers the friends-specific question that hint line was always trying to ask. The original global, self-inclusive count moved to its own new \"SN ONLINE\" Start Menu row/screen instead (see below), well away from anything friends-related, so the two numbers can no longer be confused for one another.",
      "SilphNetNearby's \"NOT YET A FRIEND\" prompt no longer overflows its 16-char/line budget. \"ADD VIA DPAD RIGHT\" was 18 characters - caught by a byte-for-byte length check while building SN ONLINE's own player-list pages (which were about to inherit the identical text), not something anyone had actually measured before. Reworded to \"RIGHT:ADD FRIEND\" (exactly 16 chars) in both places.",
      "SN ONLINE now includes you in both the summary counts and the relevant version's player list, shown as \"(YOU)\" with no add-friend prompt on your own row - it previously excluded you entirely, undercounting the true total online. The status screen's separate FRIENDS-only count is unaffected by this and still excludes you, exactly as before.",
      "Friend detail PARTY page: the 4th move line no longer sits flush against the hint row below it. Moves are now packed at 8px per line instead of 16px (each move is one short line with nothing else on its row, so the extra height was never needed) - frees three clear rows that were previously unused, restoring a visible gap above the hint line.",
      "Friend activity could silently go missing for hours despite real catches happening: a second catch arriving before the first one's upload had finished used to overwrite it in a single slot with no way to ever send it, permanently losing that activity. Replaced with a small queue (up to 5 pending) that only clears an entry once the server actually confirms it, and retries automatically if a send fails - catches during an active session are no longer lost to this race.",
      "SN ONLINE and SN NEARBY's \"NOT YET A FRIEND\" prompt no longer reads as \"press RIGHT to add this friend\" when RIGHT actually does something else on both screens (page game versions on SN ONLINE, page nearby players on SN NEARBY) - reported directly against SN ONLINE, where pressing RIGHT while viewing someone on RED ONLINE just paged to BLUE ONLINE instead of doing anything friend-related. Rather than just rewording the hint to describe going to the status screen, START (genuinely unbound on both screens) now does the real thing: it jumps straight to the Add Friend screen with that person's Trainer ID already filled into the digit spinner, so there's no retyping and the hint (\"START:ADD FRIEND\") finally names a button that does what it says. SilphNetAddFriend gained a new optional args.prefillId to support this, reusing the same args-reaching-new() mechanism SilphNetMarkerTalk already relies on.",
      "Fixed the mod failing to load entirely (\"love.thread is not available to mods\") after a Gen1Recomp engine update permanently blocked love.thread from mod code as part of a mod-sandboxing security fix. Every network request (login, presence, friends, add-friend, everything) now calls the API directly and synchronously instead of firing a background thread - confirmed directly against the engine's own sandbox source that this is the intended path (require(\"socket.http\") is still reachable with the \"network\" permission this mod already declares; only love.thread itself was cut off, with no replacement offered). The real trade-off: the game now visibly pauses for the duration of each request rather than staying fully responsive in the background - a normal fast response is unnoticeable, but the request timeout was cut from 8s to 2.5s specifically to bound how long a slow or unreachable connection can freeze the game for in the worst case.",
    },
    known = {
      "A save that's beaten the league MULTIPLE times, then gets exported/re-imported via the launcher's .sav feature, still loses the exact count (only floors back to 1 - see the EVENT_BEAT_CHAMPION_RIVAL fix above) - this is a genuine limitation of the base engine's .sav codec, which has no way to carry a roster of past Hall of Fame entries through that format at all, not something this mod can fully recover from on its own. Every real clear going forward (without a further import) still counts up normally on top of that floor.",
      "Marker sprite is fixed to SPRITE_RED for now - the gym sign and league leaderboard sign both reuse the same placeholder sprite for consistency, since no dedicated sign sprite is confirmed available yet either",
      "Gym sign / league leaderboard sign placement can occasionally fail to find a safe tile in an unusually cramped spot right at a gym's entrance (no sign spawns that visit, logged a warning) - the search deliberately never falls back to a guessed coordinate, since this project ships no ROM data",
      "Gym/league sign placement has no way to know where a gym's own statues or other NPCs stand - confirmed directly against the engine's own MapOverview.build(): the collision grid this search reads is built purely from static map tile collision, and has no idea an NPC (a statue included) is currently sitting on an otherwise-walkable tile. A real report (Viridian Gym) had the sign land right on top of one. There's no mod-facing API to list NPC positions on a map to check against, so this can't be fully prevented in general without hardcoding a specific gym's real layout, which this project deliberately never does. If this happens again, report the exact tile from the mod.log:info() line every sign spawn now writes (\"SilphNet: gym sign placed on <MAP> at (x,y)\") - that specific tile gets permanently excluded going forward (SIGN_AVOID_TILES in main.lua), rather than trying to guess harder up front.",
      "badges_mask only reflects whatever a friend's client has already uploaded since updating to this version - a friend who hasn't been online since updating shows \"NO FRIENDS HAVE THIS BADGE YET\" on a gym sign even if they really do have it, until their own client catches up (same self-reported-stats limitation every other friend stat in this mod already has)",
      "No battles, trades or chat - presence and friends only",
      "GitHub auto-update requires the repo to be reachable by the launcher (e.g. public, or however Gen1Recomp's manager handles private-repo auth) - not verified on-device yet",
      "Only 8 friend markers can be identified (pressed on for their name) at once on the same map - plenty for normal use, but raise MARKER_SLOTS in main.lua if ever needed",
      "Friend stats/activity are self-reported: a mod can only ever read its OWN game.save, so a friend's stats only show up once THEIR client has actually uploaded a snapshot - a brand new friend, or one who hasn't been online since updating to this version, shows NO STATS YET until their own client catches up.",
      "Activity currently only reports catches (real pokemon.caught event, with level from the event's own mon payload) - trainer-battle events (\"DFTD BUG CATCHER\" etc.) aren't wired up: the engine's documented events don't cleanly support this yet (world.trainer_engaged has the trainer's class but fires at battle START with no outcome; battle.ended has a result but no trainer identity) - would need to stitch the two together and hasn't been tested. Level-up/badge-earned/League-win aren't wired up either, though the same upload path (stats.php's activity field) would support them.",
    },
  },
